.TH DF 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
df \- report file system space usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B df
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B df
lists every mounted file system with its size, the space used and the
space available, in 1 KiB blocks, the share in use as a percentage,
and where it is mounted.
The first column names its source (a disk's address, or
.BR tmpfs ).
.PP
File systems that report no size, such as
.IR /dev ,
are left out.
Arguments are ignored.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ df
Filesystem     1K-blocks  Used ...
.fi
.SH NOTES
Sizes are always in KiB; there is no
.B \-h
and no file system or path argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR du (1),
.BR mount (1),
.BR free (1)
